 ### Semi-transparent Iso-surfaces
-A method that searches for ray intersections with iso-surfaces defined by specific iso-values, colors, and opacities, allowing for high-quality surface visualization and Hitpoint Refinement [S20, unofficial]. It traverses the ray and, when the ray passes across an iso-value, calculates a more exact intersection point using linear interpolation between ray positions and sampled values on current and previous steps [S20, unofficial]. Iso-surface Parameters: Each surface is defined by an iso-value, color, and opacity, adjusted via the Transfer function window [S20, unofficial]. Choose this for semi-transparent isosurface rendering with hitpoint refinement.
